From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:18:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): focus follows the HTML focusing steps

focus() gave focus to any element and fired nothing; blur() only cleared it;
activeElement exposed nodes inside shadow trees.

Only a focusable area (a link, a form control, an iframe, an element with a
tabindex, an editing host, the first summary of a details) that is rendered,
enabled and not inert takes focus, or a shadow host's focus delegate. Moving
focus fires blur and focusout on the element losing it, then focus and focusin
on the new one, with relatedTarget, in Chrome's order; a removed element loses
focus. document.activeElement and ShadowRoot.activeElement retarget.
focus() scrolls a target that is not fully in view to the centre unless
preventScroll is set.

__obscura_focusOnPress is the mouse-focus rule CDP input runs for a press
nobody cancelled: the nearest flat-tree inclusive ancestor that is a focusable
area (the editing host inside contenteditable) or a focus delegate takes
focus, and with none focus returns to the viewport.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
